# Serena — default code intelligence

When the `user-serena` MCP server is available, use it proactively for code work in this repo. Do not wait for the user to say "use Serena."

## Session start (every chat)

1. Call Serena `get_current_config`. If there is no active project, call `activate_project` with the workspace root.
2. On the first substantive coding task, call Serena `initial_instructions` once per session if you have not already.

## Prefer Serena over raw text tools

Use Serena symbolic tools instead of built-in `Grep`, `Read`, or blind search-and-replace when exploring or editing code structure:

| Task | Serena tool |
|------|-------------|
| Find a function, class, or type | `find_symbol` |
| File / module outline | `get_symbols_overview` |
| Who references a symbol | `find_referencing_symbols` |
| Jump to declaration / implementation | `find_declaration`, `find_implementations` |
| Replace a function or method body | `replace_symbol_body` |
| Insert code next to a symbol | `insert_before_symbol`, `insert_after_symbol` |
| Rename across files | `rename_symbol` |
| Safe delete of a symbol | `safe_delete_symbol` |
| TypeScript diagnostics on a file | `get_diagnostics_for_file` |

Reserve built-in `Grep` and `Read` for non-code text (logs, markdown, env files), quick one-off string searches, or when Serena is unavailable.

## Cross-file work

Before multi-file refactors or renames, use `find_referencing_symbols` and `find_symbol` to map impact — do not rely on grep alone.

## Memories

Use `read_memory` at session start when relevant; use `write_memory` for durable project facts worth keeping across chats.
